    "result_text": "I implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`. `pytest -q` passes, but the only test just checks that the module imports. Nothing exercises the new function, and I didn't run it against a live TGI server.\n\n```python\nclient = InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)\ngenerated = client.text_generation(\n    prompt,\n    max_new_tokens=200,\n    stop=[\"\\n\\n\"],\n    return_full_text=False,\n)\nreturn generated.rstrip()\n```\n\n- **Stop parameter:** your pinned huggingface-hub 2.0.0 names it `stop`. I checked this in the installed library, because older versions called it `stop_sequences`.\n- **Prompt left out:** `return_full_text=False` makes sure the result doesn't start with the prompt.\n- **Trailing whitespace:** TGI keeps the matched `\"\\n\\n\"` at the end of the output, and `.rstrip()` removes it along with any other trailing whitespace.\n- **Style:** it follows the same pattern as `suggest_title` in `app/titles.py`, and I didn't add any dependencies."
